      "statement": "start_automation and stop_automation are only called from the startup sweep, so REST or MCP create/update/delete/toggle operations persist rows without registering or removing runtime jobs; condition loops compensate by re-reading is_enabled each iteration and exiting when disabled, but already-registered cron jobs keep firing until restart because execute_automation_command never re-checks is_enabled.",
